<h1>Certificate of Practical Completion</h1>

<p style="color: var(--color-text-secondary);">
  Job: <%= @job[:job_number] %> | <%= @job[:name] %><br>
  Date: <%= format_date(today, :long) %>
</p>

<h2>Project Details</h2>

<table>
  <tr>
    <td style="width: 35%; background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>Site Address</strong></td>
    <td><%= @job[:full_address] %></td>
  </tr>
  <% if @job[:lot_number].present? %>
  <tr>
    <td style="background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>Lot/Plan</strong></td>
    <td>Lot <%= @job[:lot_number] %> on Plan <%= @job[:plan_number] %></td>
  </tr>
  <% end %>
  <tr>
    <td style="background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>Client(s)</strong></td>
    <td><%= @client_names %></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>Builder</strong></td>
    <td><%= @company[:name] %></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>QBCC Licence</strong></td>
    <td><%= @company[:qbcc_license] %></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>Contract Details</h2>

<table>
  <tr>
    <td style="width: 35%; background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>Contract Date</strong></td>
    <td><%= @job[:contract_date] %></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>Original Contract Price</strong></td>
    <td><%= @job[:contract_price] %> (inc. GST)</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>Approved Variations</strong></td>
    <td></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>Final Contract Price</strong></td>
    <td></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>Completion Details</h2>

<table>
  <tr>
    <td style="width: 35%; background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>Date of Practical Completion</strong></td>
    <td><%= format_date(today, :long) %></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>Building Approval Reference</strong></td>
    <td></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td style="background: #f5f5f5;"><strong>Final Inspection Date</strong></td>
    <td></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h2>Certification</h2>

<p>
  <strong><%= @company[:name] %></strong> (QBCC Licence No. <%= @company[:qbcc_license] %>)
  hereby certifies that:
</p>

<ol>
  <li>
    The building work described above has been completed in accordance with the
    building contract, plans, and specifications.
  </li>
  <li>
    The work has been carried out in a proper and workmanlike manner and complies
    with the Building Code of Australia and relevant Australian Standards.
  </li>
  <li>
    All required inspections have been completed and certified.
  </li>
  <li>
    The building is fit for occupation and its intended use.
  </li>
</ol>

<h2>Outstanding Items (Defects)</h2>

<p>
  The following minor items remain to be completed or rectified within 7 days:
</p>

<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 10%;">No.</th>
    <th style="width: 60%;">Description</th>
    <th>Target Date</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>1</td>
    <td></td>
    <td></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>2</td>
    <td></td>
    <td></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>3</td>
    <td></td>
    <td></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>4</td>
    <td></td>
    <td></td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td>5</td>
    <td></td>
    <td></td>
  </tr>
</table>

<p>
  <em>Note: These minor items do not affect practical completion or occupancy.</em>
</p>

<h2>Warranties</h2>

<p>
  From the date of practical completion, the following statutory warranties apply:
</p>

<ul>
  <li><strong>Structural Defects:</strong> 6 years and 6 months</li>
  <li><strong>Non-Structural Defects:</strong> 6 months</li>
  <li><strong>Subsidence or Settlement:</strong> 6 years and 6 months</li>
</ul>

<p>
  Additional manufacturer warranties may apply to specific products and systems.
  Please refer to the separate warranty documentation provided.
</p>

